          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সংবাদপত্র — sôngbādpôtrô — \"a newspaper\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বাবা প্রতিদিন সকালে সংবাদপত্র পড়েন। bābā prôtidin sôkāle sôngbādpôtrô pôṛen. Father reads the newspaper every morning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সংবাদপত্র (sôngbādpôtrô) joins Sanskrit saṃvāda, 'a speaking together, a conversation' (Monier-Williams), to pattra, 'a leaf, a written sheet': a sheet of news. Everyday speech says খবরের কাগজ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
